From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lance-context-core: drop the unused lance-graph dependency

crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml depends on `lance-graph = "0.5.4"`,
but no Rust source file in this workspace imports `lance_graph`
(`grep -rln lance_graph crates/ python/` matches nothing). lance-graph's
own Cargo.toml pins `lance`/`lance-core`/`lance-linalg` at an incompatible
`1.x` line, which Cargo resolves as a third, parallel copy of the whole
lance-core/lance-linalg family next to the `7.0.0` one lancedb pulls in
and the `9.0.0` one `crates/lance-context-core` depends on directly.
Cargo's `[patch]` table needs one entry per semver-incompatible line of a
crate that is to be redirected, and the riscv64 SIMD fallbacks (see
0003-cargo-patch-lance-crates-for-riscv64.patch) only exist for the 7.x
and 9.x lines, so removing the dead dependency drops the 1.x copy from
resolution instead.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to lance-format/lance-context]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml b/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
index a5d0f25..928c52a 100644
--- a/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/lance-context-core/Cargo.toml
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ lance-context-api = { version = "0.6.7", path = "../lance-context-api" }
 lance-index = "9.0.0"
 lance-namespace = "9.0.0"
 lancedb = "0.30.0"
-lance-graph = "0.5.4"
 # Version-matched with lance-context-server/-master so one process-wide recorder
 # serves every crate.
 metrics = { version = "0.24", optional = true }
-- 
2.43.0
